       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day under physician supervision). The single dose is also above the usual maximum of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some regimens you might have meant:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's an intentional above-maximum dose. Otherwise, tell me the regimen you'd like and I'll enter it."
